From a298af954e5e5f74f042bf3cd623ad76e4131848 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yve <yve@omnicrash.net>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 17:50:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 62/63] Audio DSP: compute mono convolutions, so TVs, phone
 calls and reverb are heard

The title sends the sound of speakers in the world (TVs, phone calls) through
the audio DSP alone, and its reverb sends through it too. The DSP's outputs
were zeros, so those were silent and reverb was dry (fxceless/victory-fork#1470).

The impulse responses the title passes to XDspActivate are blocks of 2048
floats: the unscaled 2048-point FFT of a 2048-sample window of the response,
window k covering samples (k-1)*1024..(k+1)*1024, bins 0-1023 interleaved
re/im, then a schedule block that starts with 0xFFFFACE1. Every block of the
title's responses matches its neighbours under that reading. An input block
zero-padded to 2048 samples times window k gives that block's part of the
output k blocks later, in the second half of the inverse FFT.

All the streams the title opened in a session with TVs, a phone call and
reverb were mono convolutions of 1024-frame blocks; those are computed now.
Stereo and 512-frame convolutions and the other transforms still give zeros.
VICTORY_DSP_CONVOLVE=0 turns it off; VICTORY_DSP_GAIN scales it (default 2:
the hardware's scaling is not known, and 1/2048 alone sounded quiet).

(cherry picked from commit 72a83ce7cc79c26ff7211623e380fc7f2e862f54)
